        "id": 1147264
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-30T22:35:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The timeout is to protect access to run the git command at L347.\nI\u0027d be quite surprised if there are so many processes waiting for the execution of `git cat-file` and 20 secs were not enough.\n\nWould you be able to confirm that they all timed out in this stage?\ni.e., they were waiting to run `git cat-file ..` but there were too many processes wanting to execute the git command such that 20 secs were not long enough to have a chance to execute the git command.\n\nwas it like more than 20 processes waiting for it?",
      "parentUuid": "af05c548_331f63d0",
      "revId": "05ca8c646ac6f807eb0143faebea0ee13192854f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af554dd5_72bbab6f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1147264
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-30T22:42:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Or, the issue could be that new processes keep coming up and down but there is no guarantee that which process will be waken up first. Therefore, it\u0027s possible that some unlucky processes hit the timeout.\n\nThen, a correct patch would more be like, providing ordered wake up. by lock+queue. If you were suffering from such a problem, then doubling the timeout would just reduce the chance, and you may end up 5x or 10x the timeout.",
      "parentUuid": "bbb882fd_671f2d85",
      "revId": "05ca8c646ac6f807eb0143faebea0ee13192854f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
